# NZ Class M — ALES 200, NDC format                     seed definition, draft
# Rule refs: NZMAA Flying Rules, Section 5: Soaring, March 2024 (NZ.3.12.7,
#            which incorporates NZ.3.12.1–3.12.6 except for the scoring)
#
# NZ.3.12.7 is the National Decentralized Contest format of the same rulebook
# class as 80-nz-m-ales200.class. It fixes the round count at four, fixes the
# target time at ten minutes, and — the reason it cannot be a parameter binding
# on the parent — scores "the sum of the four rounds RAW scores", with no
# normalisation at all.
#
# That is a different pipeline, not a different number, so it is a different
# CompetitionClass. Additive, and consistent with the law in CLAUDE.md. The
# cost is recorded in notation §12: nothing in the model says these two
# definitions are one class in the rulebook.
#
# It exercises F25 (no `normalise`) alongside 83/85, and is the one place a
# maximum score is stated outright, which makes it a good arithmetic check.

class NZ-M-NDC
  name     "ALES 200 (NDC format)"
  fai      ""
  version  "NZMAA Section 5 Soaring, March 2024"

  # No targetTime parameter: NZ.3.12.7 a fixes the rounds at "4 rounds, each of
  # 10 minutes", so the parent's CD discretion (NZ.3.12.1 g) does not apply and
  # the turning point is a rule constant again.

  param minNewGroup no default                                   # NZ.3.12.5 l states no minimum for a
                                                                 #   re-flight group (F12), as the parent

  # no finalRanking: one phase, so SinglePhase (NZ.3.12.7 has no fly-off)

  reflight
    entitled     UndefinedRequiresRuling                         # NZ.3.12.5 l, as the parent
    others       UndefinedRequiresRuling                         # NZ.3.12.5 l
    minNewGroup  param(minNewGroup)                              # NZ.3.12.5 l, as the parent (F12)

  penalty "launchOutsideBuzzerWindow" zeroRound                  # NZ.3.12.1 h
  penalty "landedOutsideFieldBounds"  zeroRound                  # NZ.3.12.4 a
  penalty "launchHeightExceeded"      zeroRound                  # NZ.2.8.3 (discretionary — see the parent)

  phase Preliminary

    rounds    FixedSequence tasksPerRound 1 maxRounds 4          # NZ.3.12.7 a "an NDC contest will comprise 4 rounds"
    validity  minRounds 4                                        # NZ.3.12.7 a
    # no drop: NZ.3.12.7 c "the sum of the four rounds"

    task D "Thermal Duration (NDC)"
      metric flightTime          Number s Truncate 1             # NZ.3.12.3 a
      metric landingDistance     Number m Ceiling  1             # NZ.2.4.5
      metric significantDamage   Flag                            # NZ.3.12.2 d
      metric touchedByCompetitor Flag                            # NZ.3.12.2 e
      metric landedWithin75m     Flag                            # NZ.2.4.6

      flights   last                                             # NZ.1.6
      timing    UntilAllFlightsComplete maxLaunches 1            # NZ.3.12.1 h
      # no group: NZ.3.12.7 c scores raw, so nothing in this task reads the
      #   group — it affects the running order and never a score

      # NO `normalise` (F25). NZ.3.12.7 c: "for NDC only, scoring will be the
      # sum of the four rounds Raw Scores." Because nothing normalises, the
      # landing bonus belongs in the RAW score here — the parent's `score
      # normalised` block would have no stage to land at, and adoption rejects
      # it. Same rulebook class, opposite answer to F24's question.

      flightValidWhen landedWithin75m == true                    # NZ.2.4.6

      score
        piecewise flightTime                                     # NZ.3.12.3 b
          0..600    @  1 pt/s                                    # NZ.3.12.7 a 10 minute target;
                                                                 #   NZ.3.12.7 c i "flight time max is 10min (600 points)"
          600..any  @ -1 pt/s                                    # NZ.3.12.1 n
        when all(significantDamage   == false,                   # NZ.3.12.2 d
                 touchedByCompetitor == false)                   # NZ.3.12.2 e
          then lookup landingDistance                            # NZ.3.12.2 b, table at NZ.2.4.5
                 <=  1 -> 50 ;  <=  2 -> 45 ;  <=  3 -> 40 ;  <=  4 -> 35
                 <=  5 -> 30 ;  <=  6 -> 25 ;  <=  7 -> 20 ;  <=  8 -> 15
                 <=  9 -> 10 ;  <= 10 ->  5 ;  any   ->  0

# ---- arithmetic check ----------------------------------------------------
# NZ.3.12.7 c states its own maxima, which is rare and useful:
#   "Flight time max is 10min (600 points) plus landing max of 50. Max round
#    score of 650."  ->  600 + 50 = 650, per the score block above.
#   "Max NDC score is 2600 points"  ->  4 x 650 = 2600, per maxRounds 4 and
#    no discard, with no normalisation to rescale it.
# Any evaluator that does not produce 2600 for four perfect rounds has either
# normalised something or applied a discard.

# ---- unresolved for NZ Class M (NDC) -------------------------------------
# 1. Tie-break: NZ.3.12.7 states none. Finding F15.
# 2. The relationship to 80-nz-m-ales200.class is unmodelled — see notation §12.
